A. Root Cause Classification
Primary
P1 — Inconsistent front_clear_center threshold (the single biggest bug) LocalPerception.update() computes self.perception.front_center_clear using CORNER_GLANCE_CENTER_CLEAR_M = 0.115. But _compute_motion_command() ignored that field and re-computed front_clear_center = (fc is None or fc > 0.14) — a completely different, harder threshold.

Evidence from log6: corner_glance_left_escape fires correctly on 6 consecutive cycles while front drops 0.169 → 0.143. On the 7th step front = 0.138. Since 0.138 < 0.14, the local re-computed front_clear_center became False, so front_corner_left (which requires front_clear_center) became False, and corner_glance silently exited — handing control back to waypoint_follow. Waypoint then drove the robot from front=0.138 all the way to front=0.049 (the hard jam threshold), triggering the full recovery sequence.

P2 — Corridor mode has no hard near-wall inhibit corridor_mode fires whenever side_near (either side < 0.13 m) AND front_open, with no floor below it. With left = 0.050, the balance formula computes wall_turn = clamp(2.025, ±1.256) = 1.256, giving cmdL=3.768, cmdR=6.280 — a ~0.60 ratio arc. This arc is too gentle to escape quickly, and the balance cap (0.20 * max_ws) prevents a stronger correction from being applied. The first ~25 log lines are the robot inching away from 0.050 toward 0.132 at this slow rate before the corner appears.

Secondary
S3 — Corner glance is not latched; exits as soon as perception condition drops The previous corner_glance code had no minimum-duration latch. If front_corner_left became False for even one step (e.g., due to sensor noise or the threshold bug above), the escape arc exited immediately. One bad sensor reading was enough to abort the manoeuvre.

S4 — Recovery turn direction uses arbitrary recovery_state % 2 parity The first recovery correctly turned right (away from the left wall, because recovery_state = 1 → parity odd → cmdL=−turn, cmdR=+turn). But if a second recovery fired, parity would flip to 0 → cmdL=+turn, cmdR=−turn → turn left, directly into the left wall. This is latent but dangerous in corner-trap cycles.

Minor
M5 — post_turn_forward corner abort threshold: fc straddles the two checks hard_front_now = (fc <= POST_TURN_ABORT_CENTER_M=0.040) OR (front_r <= POST_TURN_ABORT_FRONT_M=0.060). With fc=0.049, the centre check fails (0.049 > 0.040) but the front-range check correctly catches it. The abort does fire, but only just — leaving a very narrow band where the robot approaches the wall at near-jam proximity. (In this run it resolved correctly, but with sensor noise it might not.)

